  "author_association": "NONE",
  "body": "### Feature Request: Create an official Discord server for the BitNet community\n\n**Description**\n\nHi team,\n\nBitNet b1.58 and bitnet.cpp are getting a lot of interest from the community, especially among people who run models on CPU, edge devices, and those who want to try Falcon3-10B 1.58-bit, other ternary models, Open WebUI integration, etc.\n\nRight now there is **no official Discord server** from Microsoft.  \nPeople are scattered across:\n- GitHub Discussions\n- r/LocalLLaMA\n- random unofficial Discords (kyegomez, some YouTube creators, etc.)\n\nIt would be very helpful to have one **official Discord** where we can:\n- Ask quick questions about building bitnet.cpp\n- Share working GGUF files for new 1.58-bit models (Falcon, future bigger models, etc.)\n- Discuss integration with Open WebUI, LM Studio, SillyTavern\n- Report bugs and share performance results on different hardware\n- Coordinate community contributions\n\nWould Microsoft consider creating an official Discord server for the BitNet project?\n\nThank you!",
